{"session_id":"svc-1778536095953135502","seq":0,"type":"session.start","ts":"2026-05-11T21:48:26.107491417Z","data":{"provider":"","model":"sonnet","sticky":{"key_present":true,"bonus":0},"utilization":{"observed_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z"},"requested_harness":"claude","resolved_harness":"claude","harness_source":"request_harness","requested_model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","resolved_model":"sonnet","work_dir":"/var/tmp/ddx-exec-wt/.execute-bead-wt-fizeau-8f62bcbb-20260511T214813-c20ca271","max_iterations":0,"prompt":"\u003cexecute-bead\u003e\n  \u003cinstructions\u003e\nYou are executing one bead inside an isolated DDx execution worktree. The bead\u0026#39;s \u0026lt;description\u0026gt; and \u0026lt;acceptance\u0026gt; are the completion contract — every AC must be provably satisfied by a specific code, test, or file you can point to after your commit.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Step 0: size check\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Too big if any holds:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- More than ~6 ACs spanning unrelated subsystems.\u0026#xA;- AC mixes design, implementation, integration tests, and docs as separate deliverables.\u0026#xA;- Description names multiple feature-sized sub-pieces.\u0026#xA;- More than ~500 lines across ~5+ files in unrelated packages.\u0026#xA;- If the bead description exceeds 8000 bytes, treat Step 0 as a split-first pass.\u0026#xA;- Auto-decomposition is capped at depth 2: root beads may split once, decomposed children once more; third-level splits must be rejected with an explanation.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;If too big, decompose — do not attempt the work:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;1. `ddx bead create` for each child slice (copy parent\u0026#39;s labels and spec-id).\u0026#xA;2. `ddx bead dep add \u0026lt;child-id\u0026gt; \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt;` to record edges.\u0026#xA;3. `ddx bead update \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt; --notes \u0026#39;decomposed into \u0026lt;child-ids\u0026gt;\u0026#39;`.\u0026#xA;4. Write `.ddx/executions/20260511T214813-c20ca271/no_changes_rationale.txt` listing child IDs, then stop.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;A clean decomposition is a success. Do not mix implementation with decomposition.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## How to work\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Read first. If the bead names files, specs, or prior beads, read them before editing — do not guess.\u0026#xA;- Cross-reference each AC against concrete evidence (test name, file path, function) before committing. If you cannot point at it, it is not done.\u0026#xA;- Run the project\u0026#39;s test and lint commands before committing. **Do not commit red code** — fix failures first.\u0026#xA;- Stage with `git add \u0026lt;specific-paths\u0026gt;`; never `git add -A` (the worktree may have unrelated WIP).\u0026#xA;- Commit exactly once when green; conventional-commit subject ending with `[\u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt;]`. Stop after the commit.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s scope.\u0026#xA;- If you cannot finish, write `.ddx/executions/20260511T214813-c20ca271/no_changes_rationale.txt` (what is done, what blocks, what a follow-up needs) before exiting. No commit and no rationale ⇒ DDx records `no_evidence_produced`. A well-justified no_changes beats a bad commit.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## no_changes contract\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;`.ddx/executions/20260511T214813-c20ca271/no_changes_rationale.txt` must contain one:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- `verification_command: \u0026lt;cmd\u0026gt;` — repo cwd; exit 0 closes, nonzero rejects.\u0026#xA;- `status: open` + `reason: \u0026lt;retryable\u0026gt;` — open, smart retry.\u0026#xA;- `status: proposed` + `reason: \u0026lt;operator needed\u0026gt;` — operator lane.\u0026#xA;- `status: blocked` + `reason: \u0026lt;external blocker\u0026gt;` — blocked lane.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;No pseudo-statuses. Bare rationales and `status: needs_investigation` reject.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;To request orchestrator decomposition, add `orchestrator_action: decompose` alongside `status: open`.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Reports\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Freestanding artifacts (investigation reports, findings docs) go under `.ddx/executions/20260511T214813-c20ca271/` (the per-attempt evidence directory under `.ddx/executions/`). **Never write reports to `/tmp` or any path outside the repository** — out-of-repo paths are invisible to the post-merge reviewer and cause BLOCK on missing evidence. If the bead names a specific in-repo path, use it; else default to `.ddx/executions/20260511T214813-c20ca271/\u0026lt;short-name\u0026gt;.md`. Stage and commit the report alongside code.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Mode and overrides\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;DDX_MODE=bead_execution: edit code/docs for bead AC. Only broad queue-steward default is overridden; tracker, merge-policy, verification, safety stay active. Bead description/AC override CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, and project defaults.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Review gate\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- The review is a gate, not an escape hatch — meet every AC in this pass.\u0026#xA;- Address every BLOCKING `\u0026lt;review-findings\u0026gt;` item; do not declare `no_changes` with blocking findings open.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Constraints\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Work only inside this execution worktree.\u0026#xA;- Keep `.ddx/executions/` intact — DDx uses it as execution evidence.\u0026#xA;- **Never run `ddx init`** — the workspace is initialized; running it corrupts the bead queue.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s named scope.\u0026#xA;- Do not rewrite CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, or other project-instructions files unless the bead asks.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## When the work is done\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;After the commit succeeds and every AC is verified, stop. Return control to the orchestrator — do not keep exploring or testing.\n  \u003c/instructions\u003e\n  \u003cbead id=\"fizeau-8f62bcbb\"\u003e\n    \u003ctitle\u003eDerive reasoning_tokens from reasoning_content when usage.completion_tokens_details is absent\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cdescription\u003e\nToday the reasoning-token extractor in `internal/sdk/openaicompat/client.go`\u0026#xA;(`extractReasoningTokens`) reads only from\u0026#xA;`usage.completion_tokens_details.reasoning_tokens` in the response body. ds4\u0026#xA;and some other providers do thinking but do NOT populate that field — they\u0026#xA;return the thinking inline as `message.reasoning_content` with no separate\u0026#xA;token-count accounting.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Verified 2026-05-11 against ds4 (vidar:1236): a simple \u0026#34;What is 17 times\u0026#xA;24?\u0026#34; prompt returned `message.reasoning_content` of 92 chars but\u0026#xA;`usage.completion_tokens_details` was absent entirely. Result: report.json\u0026#xA;records reasoning_tokens=0 for every ds4 cell even when thinking ran for\u0026#xA;thousands of tokens.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Per ADR-010 Amendment §8, the resolution chain must be:\u0026#xA;1. If usage.completion_tokens_details.reasoning_tokens is present, use it.\u0026#xA;2. Else if message.reasoning_content is non-empty, derive an approximation\u0026#xA;   from char-count / 4. Annotate with reasoning_tokens_approx=true.\u0026#xA;3. Else reasoning_tokens=0 (honest zero, not silent truncation).\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Implementation:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;1. Extend `extractReasoningTokens` in\u0026#xA;   `internal/sdk/openaicompat/client.go` to take both the raw usage JSON\u0026#xA;   AND the raw message JSON (or refactor to read message.reasoning_content\u0026#xA;   from the parsed response if it\u0026#39;s already structured).\u0026#xA;2. Apply the char-count fallback when usage path is absent AND\u0026#xA;   message.reasoning_content is non-empty.\u0026#xA;3. Add a new boolean field `ReasoningTokensApprox` to\u0026#xA;   `internal/core/agent.go` `TokenUsage` struct. Default false.\u0026#xA;4. Wire ReasoningTokensApprox through into the matrix runner\u0026#39;s report.json\u0026#xA;   (`cmd/bench/matrix.go` — alongside the existing ReasoningTokens\u0026#xA;   plumbing).\u0026#xA;5. The char-count/4 estimator is a v1 placeholder; a future bead can\u0026#xA;   replace with a real tokenizer (tiktoken-go or model-specific) if\u0026#xA;   needed. Document the v1 method in the field\u0026#39;s GoDoc.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Test cases (table-driven in\u0026#xA;`internal/sdk/openaicompat/client_test.go`):\u0026#xA;- usage path present, reasoning_content also present → use usage (more\u0026#xA;  authoritative; report approx=false).\u0026#xA;- usage path absent, reasoning_content present (92 chars) → derive 23\u0026#xA;  tokens (92/4). approx=true.\u0026#xA;- both absent → 0, approx=false.\u0026#xA;- usage path = 0 (explicit zero), reasoning_content present → still use\u0026#xA;  usage\u0026#39;s zero (caller signaled no reasoning); approx=false. NOTE: this\u0026#xA;  is a judgment call; document it.\u0026#xA;- Streaming path: aggregate reasoning_content across deltas, char-count\u0026#xA;  the aggregated string.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;In-scope files:\u0026#xA;- internal/sdk/openaicompat/client.go\u0026#xA;- internal/sdk/openaicompat/client_test.go (new tests)\u0026#xA;- internal/core/agent.go (add ReasoningTokensApprox field to TokenUsage)\u0026#xA;- cmd/bench/matrix.go (extend report.json to carry the approx flag)\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Out-of-scope:\u0026#xA;- Real tokenizer integration (tiktoken-go etc.) — v1 uses chars/4. Filed\u0026#xA;  as a follow-up after we have measurements on how much approx error\u0026#xA;  matters in practice.\u0026#xA;- Streaming-specific token-counting optimizations.\n    \u003c/description\u003e\n    \u003cacceptance\u003e\n1. `go test ./internal/sdk/openaicompat/...` passes including the five\u0026#xA;   table cases above.\u0026#xA;2. `go test ./internal/core/...` passes; the TokenUsage struct round-trips\u0026#xA;   ReasoningTokensApprox through JSON.\u0026#xA;3. `go test ./cmd/bench/...` passes; report.json carries\u0026#xA;   reasoning_tokens_approx alongside reasoning_tokens.\u0026#xA;4. Manual smoke: send a chat completion to ds4 vidar:1236 with\u0026#xA;   `reasoning_effort: high`, parse the response with the updated extractor,\u0026#xA;   verify the resulting TokenUsage has Reasoning \u0026gt; 0 and\u0026#xA;   ReasoningTokensApprox == true.\u0026#xA;5. `go vet ./...` passes.\n    \u003c/acceptance\u003e\n    \u003clabels\u003earea:provider, area:reasoning, area:telemetry, kind:bug\u003c/labels\u003e\n    \u003cmetadata spec-id=\"ADR-010\" base-rev=\"12ecdd4ee28a9f63021a8e1d9d57672d8e3ecac4\" bundle=\".ddx/executions/20260511T214813-c20ca271\"/\u003e\n  \u003c/bead\u003e\n  \u003cgoverning\u003e\n    \u003cref id=\"ADR-010\" path=\"docs/helix/02-design/adr/ADR-010-reasoning-wire-form-from-catalog.md\"\u003eADR-010: Reasoning Wire Form Belongs in the Model Catalog\u003c/ref\u003e\n  \u003c/governing\u003e\n\u003c/execute-bead\u003e\n","metadata":{"DDX_MODE":"bead_execution","attempt_id":"20260511T214813-c20ca271","base_rev":"12ecdd4ee28a9f63021a8e1d9d57672d8e3ecac4","bead_id":"fizeau-8f62bcbb","bundle_path":".ddx/executions/20260511T214813-c20ca271","correlation_id":"fizeau-8f62bcbb:20260511T214813-c20ca271","prompt_file":".ddx/executions/20260511T214813-c20ca271/prompt.md","prompt_sha":"9edac9f03df2223ca48bd424f271c7a04f5be2e33a7a38f3dfaadb78dbbc37d6","role":"implementer","session_id":"eb-eaf2bebc","worker_id":""}}}
